## 7. Required Test Fixtures and Scenarios

Create or update tests/fixtures using synthetic, non-sensitive data. Cover each affected document type.

### Content and layout

- Normal short invoice/quotation.
- Long company and customer names.
- Multi-line addresses and contact details.
- Long project titles and descriptions.
- Many materials/labor rows or equivalent document items.
- Long notes, scope, warranty, and terms.
- Missing optional contact details.
- Missing logo and local-font fallback.
- Zero subtotal/category totals.
- Zero tax and zero discount when those fields are supported.
- Missing tax/discount when not provided.
- Negative/adjustment values if supported by current business rules.
- Long tables spanning at least two pages.
- Missing optional sections with no empty visual shells.

### Financial correctness

- Currency formatting and decimal precision.
- Displayed subtotal and grand total matching the validated document data.
- Tax/discount rows matching the supported data contract.
- No hidden zero values due to truthiness checks.
- No accidental currency label changes or recomputation in the template.

### Rendering and assets

- Actual PDF generation succeeds.
- Logo loads from the intended path and maintains aspect ratio.
- Fonts load locally or fall back acceptably offline.
- No clipped text, overlapping totals, or unexpected blank pages.
- Page size and margins are correct.
- Browser preview styling does not leak undesirably into printed output.

Do not report a rendering check as passed if only the HTML/CSS was inspected. Generate a real PDF with the project's available renderer and inspect its pages visually or using the available PDF QA tools.

